# BubblinCrude — audited state and backlog

Verified counts: **334 streams, 347 sites, 155 hubs, 773 refineries.**
Streams are clean — zero broken `related_ids`/`site_ids`/`hub_ids`, no duplicate
ids, yields sum to 100±10, TBP curves monotonic. Coverage: 100% api/sulfur/yields/
notes, 88% TAN, 63% distillation+resid, 61% metals, 5% SARA. `cuts` and `products`
are complete — do not "improve" them without a specific reason.

Never hand-edit the version; use `scripts/bump-version.py` and `--check`.

## 1. Refinery layer — capacity filled from Climate TRACE; keep matching conservative

574 of 773 have `capacity_kbd` (US from EIA-820, others from Climate TRACE v7
`oil-and-gas-refining`, CC BY 4.0). Rebuild via `scripts/build-refineries.py`.
Attaching a real capacity to the wrong plant is worse than leaving it null.

Still open: 199 plants with no kb/d, many without `operator`, and **none** have
`related_ids`, so refineries still do not link to streams. OSM junk roads/rails/
power pins and the five country errors (Panipat, Xinjiang, Isaac Sabbá, Soraz,
CNPC Niger) were fixed in the TRACE rebuild.

## 2. Blend calculator — data already supports it

See the `crude-blend-math` rule. 334/334 streams are blendable.

## 3. Phone filters

`styles.css` hides `.rail-filters` below 1100px with no JS fallback, so phone and
tablet lose sulfur class, region, kind, completeness, and all four saved views.
Put them in a bottom sheet. Note `sizeMapToBelt()` derives map height from *width*
alone, so topbar changes cost inspector scroll, never map size.

## 4. Marker clustering

Every pin is a `divIcon` (2 DOM nodes, 4px dot in a 28px hit box), all destroyed
and rebuilt per filter change — ~1470 nodes on Refineries. Hit boxes overlap
several deep in Europe, so precise tapping is impossible. Clustering fixes
density, tap accuracy, and perf together.

## 5. Small items

- `#has-distill` is a no-op: it tests `s.yields || s.distillation_curve` and all
  334 have `yields`. Point it at `distillation_curve` only (211) or delete it.
- `applySavedView()` hardcodes per-id special cases duplicating the declarative
  `filters` in `data.js`, plus a `hasResid` branch matching no real filter key.
  Delete them so editing `data.js` alone works.
- Three `source` strings leak drafting notes: `brent` ("paste truncated"),
  `harding` ("date not in paste"), `ea-blend` ("quality fair").
- 85 streams have `year: 2026` which is retrieval date, not sample date (67 are
  CrudeMonitor). Split retrieved vs sampled.
- No `robots.txt`, `sitemap.xml`, or JSON-LD (the hub has JSON-LD; the app doesn't).
- Hubs are 143/155 `loading` with only 4 `pricing`, so the role legend is nearly
  monochrome. **Midland is missing** despite WTI Midland joining Dated Brent in 2023.
- `#search-results` aria-label is always "Matching streams" and `#map` is always
  "World map of crude streams", regardless of active layer.
